course: dictionary
lesson: 1339
title: Camouflage: blending in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Camouflage is colours, patterns or shapes that help something blend into its surroundings, so it is hard to see. Read the sentence around the word to find its meaning. «A child in a green jumper hiding in a hedge» is hard to find at hide-and-seek because the green matches the leaves.
explain: To camouflage means to hide something by making it look like what is around it. «Birds ate the stick insects that looked least like twigs.» The insects that looked like twigs lived longer, so camouflage here means looking like the twigs and plants nearby.
explain: Camouflage can also be a noun for clothing. Soldiers wear camouflage, which is green and brown so that it blends in with the land. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «The soldiers wore green and brown camouflage» still make sense? It does, so you have understood it.
fact: Camouflage means colours, patterns or shapes that help something blend into its surroundings.
fact: To camouflage means to hide something by making it look like what is around it.
fact: Stick insects use camouflage to look like twigs, and chameleons can change colour to hide.
fact: «Their black and white suits are camouflage» means the colours help them match their surroundings.
fact: Camouflage is useful for hiding from predators, or for sneaking up on prey.
exercise: «Their black and white suits are camouflage: from below a white belly matches the bright sky.» What does camouflage mean here? | *Colours that help them blend into their surroundings | Shiny metal plates | Clothes for cold weather | Bright colours that show from far away
exercise: The stick insect will ___ itself as a twig. Choose the right word. | shout | *camouflage | melt | celebrate
exercise: «A child in a green jumper hiding in a hedge» is hard to find. Why? | The child is very tall | The jumper is shiny | *The green matches the hedge | The hedge is on fire
test: Which animal can change its colour as camouflage? | Goat | Horse | Elephant | *Chameleon
test: Why is a polar bear's white fur useful? | *It matches the snow so the bear is hard to see | It is easy for hunters to spot | It makes the bear glow in the dark | It keeps the bear dry in summer
exam: What does «camouflaged» mean in the phrase «camouflaged against the rocks»? | *Hidden by looking like the rocks | Standing very tall above the rocks | Turned into a rock | Painted bright red
